WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.569
-My first guest is a very
talented actor and producer

00:00:03.569 --> 00:00:05.572
who's written
this new children's book

00:00:05.572 --> 00:00:08.274
called "The One
and Only Sparkella,"

00:00:08.274 --> 00:00:09.842
which is available now.

00:00:09.842 --> 00:00:12.378
Here is Channing Tatum!

00:00:12.378 --> 00:00:14.180
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:16.115
Wow, that's --

00:00:16.115 --> 00:00:17.984
That's what I'm
talking about, buddy.

00:00:17.984 --> 00:00:19.919
Oh, it's so good to see you.

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:21.553
-Good to see you, too, bro.
What's up?

00:00:21.553 --> 00:00:22.655
-I missed you, buddy.

00:00:22.655 --> 00:00:24.423
Thank you so much
for coming on the show.

00:00:24.423 --> 00:00:25.958
It's great to see you.

00:00:25.958 --> 00:00:27.393
You look fantastic.

00:00:27.393 --> 00:00:28.594
-Thanks, man.

00:00:28.594 --> 00:00:31.398
-I got to say, a lot of people
have talked about

00:00:31.398 --> 00:00:33.933
gaining weight
during this pandemic.

00:00:33.933 --> 00:00:37.403
You've actually gotten
in better shape than ever.

00:00:37.403 --> 00:00:38.604
-I did, I did. You know,

00:00:38.604 --> 00:00:41.174
for the first like
I'd say week or two weeks,

00:00:41.174 --> 00:00:43.710
I definitely was just drinking
beers and riding dirt bikes.

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:46.579
And I was like, "I can't do this
for like two months.

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:48.014
Like, this is bad."

00:00:48.014 --> 00:00:50.282
And then me and my buddy, we
just went really, really hard.

00:00:50.282 --> 00:00:52.218
We just started training
every day.

00:00:52.218 --> 00:00:53.519
And it was great.

00:00:53.519 --> 00:00:56.322
I mean, I came out
a completely new person.

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:57.723
-Yeah. I --

00:00:57.723 --> 00:01:01.093
How big did you get drinking
beers and riding dirt bikes?

00:01:01.093 --> 00:01:03.430
-Pretty fat,
I would say probably,

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:05.998
you know, college 10,
a nice 10 pounds.

00:01:05.998 --> 00:01:07.299
And then I took it off.

00:01:07.299 --> 00:01:10.269
-Yeah. I saw you posted
this photo right here.

00:01:10.269 --> 00:01:13.740
It said, "Daddy is finally back.
Let's go."

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:17.476
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:17.476 --> 00:01:18.978
It's like looking in a mirror.

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:21.648
It's really --
For me, it's so bizarre.

00:01:21.648 --> 00:01:23.616
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.616 --> 00:01:27.987
But you -- You got in shape
for this movie "Dog."

00:01:27.987 --> 00:01:29.422
-Yeah.
-Is that right? Now, this is --

00:01:29.422 --> 00:01:32.058
You produced this
but also directed this

00:01:32.058 --> 00:01:33.993
or co-directed this. What --

00:01:33.993 --> 00:01:35.828
-Yeah. I don't know
if I'll be doing that again.

00:01:35.828 --> 00:01:36.962
If I ever direct again,

00:01:36.962 --> 00:01:38.598
I definitely won't
be in the movie.

00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:40.699
And we were like the first of

00:01:40.699 --> 00:01:43.169
I think there was three movies
that got going right after

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:45.104
the first quarantine,
so we were the Guinea pigs

00:01:45.104 --> 00:01:47.207
of trying to figure out
the protocols and everything.

00:01:47.207 --> 00:01:48.641
We were just burning money.

00:01:48.641 --> 00:01:50.309
-Oh, my God.
-But we got through it.

00:01:50.309 --> 00:01:53.546
I only got bit like six
or seven times by the dogs.

00:01:53.546 --> 00:01:56.516
So it was fun.
It was a great experience.

00:01:56.516 --> 00:01:58.250
-Yeah, of course it is.
-I would love to do it again.

00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:01.921
-Yeah. You're about to do
a movie with Sandra Bullock.

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:03.956
-Yeah.
-And that I'm excited about.

00:02:03.956 --> 00:02:05.725
She is --
She's awesome, by the way.

00:02:05.725 --> 00:02:07.227
Have you worked with her before?

00:02:07.227 --> 00:02:08.294
-I've never worked with her.

00:02:08.294 --> 00:02:10.796
Our kids went
to preschool together,

00:02:10.796 --> 00:02:12.632
and that was like the most --

00:02:12.632 --> 00:02:14.634
You get to understand
really quickly

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:16.835
why she is
at the level that she is.

00:02:16.835 --> 00:02:19.472
She's so smart.
She's so engaged.

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:21.407
She's producing this thing,
so I just get to show up

00:02:21.407 --> 00:02:24.310
and try to remember my lines
and not get bit by her

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:25.811
and --
[ Laughter ]

00:02:25.811 --> 00:02:28.981
-Yeah, hopefully, you don't get
bit again on this movie, yeah.

00:02:28.981 --> 00:02:31.284
I want to talk about
your children's book here.

00:02:31.284 --> 00:02:34.854
This is
"The One and Only Sparkella."

00:02:34.854 --> 00:02:37.457
I loved it. I can't wait
to read it to my daughters.

00:02:37.457 --> 00:02:38.658
-That's awesome.

00:02:38.658 --> 00:02:41.260
-Was this inspired
by your daughter?

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:43.296
-Yeah. You know,
my daughter, Everly,

00:02:43.296 --> 00:02:45.398
she's just such
a little contrarian.

00:02:45.398 --> 00:02:48.668
And since she was like a baby,
she would always just go to

00:02:48.668 --> 00:02:51.504
the most colorful thing, to
the most magical-looking thing.

00:02:51.504 --> 00:02:53.339
And she liked
to wear funny things

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:54.540
that would make people laugh.

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:57.709
And then one day,
I remember we were in preschool,

00:02:57.709 --> 00:03:00.980
and she had this, like, cape,
this watermelon cape.

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:02.649
When you held your arms
out like this,

00:03:02.649 --> 00:03:04.149
you look like
a slice of watermelon.

00:03:04.149 --> 00:03:06.185
And she just thought it was
the funniest thing in the world.

00:03:06.185 --> 00:03:09.055
And when we were about to go
to preschool this one morning,

00:03:09.055 --> 00:03:11.056
she got really self-conscious
when we were about to leave

00:03:11.056 --> 00:03:12.358
and wanted to take it off.

00:03:12.358 --> 00:03:13.559
And I was like,
"What's going on?"

00:03:13.559 --> 00:03:14.927
And she's like,
"I don't want to get laughed at.

00:03:14.927 --> 00:03:16.195
I don't want people
to laugh at me."

00:03:16.195 --> 00:03:17.964
And it sort of broke my heart,

00:03:17.964 --> 00:03:20.099
'cause I had never seen her
be self-conscious

00:03:20.099 --> 00:03:23.869
or aware even
of other people's perspectives.

00:03:23.869 --> 00:03:27.440
And it was beautiful
to, like, know

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:29.475
that I got to be there for her
and kind of help her through it.

00:03:29.475 --> 00:03:31.644
And that's kind of
where the book came from.

00:03:31.644 --> 00:03:33.512
And just like for dads,
you know --

00:03:33.512 --> 00:03:36.048
I was really nervous
to be a girl dad.

00:03:36.048 --> 00:03:38.651
First thing I did when I figured
I was going to have a girl,

00:03:38.651 --> 00:03:40.552
I literally went to YouTube
and learned how to braid hair,

00:03:40.552 --> 00:03:41.988
just 'cause I didn't
want to be that dad

00:03:41.988 --> 00:03:44.323
that dropped their kid off --
-Dude, me, too. I bought a book.

00:03:44.323 --> 00:03:45.691
I bought a book
on braiding hair.

00:03:45.691 --> 00:03:46.926
-Yeah.
-I had no idea.

00:03:46.926 --> 00:03:49.662
-It's not easy,
and it takes a long time.

00:03:49.662 --> 00:03:51.998
The hardest thing is getting
the three equal strands.

00:03:51.998 --> 00:03:53.665
-Yes, yes, no, yes, I know.

00:03:53.665 --> 00:03:55.701
It's -- Yes. It's unbelievable.

00:03:55.701 --> 00:03:57.904
-Then they make it harder
with, like, layered hair,

00:03:57.904 --> 00:03:59.072
and you're just like, "Uh."

00:03:59.072 --> 00:04:00.339
And then you would
get halfway through it,

00:04:00.339 --> 00:04:01.974
and you're realizing
one is way too short

00:04:01.974 --> 00:04:03.476
and you have to start all over.

00:04:03.476 --> 00:04:04.710
It's silly.

00:04:04.710 --> 00:04:07.046
-I think you're
a pretty awesome dad.

00:04:07.046 --> 00:04:09.882
That's the one thing I did like,
too, at the beginning here, too,

00:04:09.882 --> 00:04:12.551
you kind of say, "Hey,
for any dads out there,

00:04:12.551 --> 00:04:15.654
this is just a --
Just be with your daughter

00:04:15.654 --> 00:04:17.156
and actually get to know her."

00:04:17.156 --> 00:04:21.527
And you posted this
on Instagram.

00:04:21.527 --> 00:04:24.730
It made me laugh.
And this is like --

00:04:24.730 --> 00:04:25.864
-Oh, no.

00:04:25.864 --> 00:04:27.567
-I've never done
quite this, but --

00:04:27.567 --> 00:04:28.835
[ Laughter ]

00:04:28.835 --> 00:04:31.371
This is a blindfold makeup?

00:04:31.371 --> 00:04:33.506
What do you do with Everly?

00:04:33.506 --> 00:04:34.773
-Yeah, we --

00:04:34.773 --> 00:04:36.241
Look, we --
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:36.241 --> 00:04:38.778
-I am subjected
to all kinds of things.

00:04:38.778 --> 00:04:40.713
But that is actually weirdly

00:04:40.713 --> 00:04:42.748
one of my favorite games
that we play.

00:04:42.748 --> 00:04:44.684
I know this might be shocking.

00:04:44.684 --> 00:04:47.053
But you literally
blindfold each other,

00:04:47.053 --> 00:04:48.954
and then you do
the other person's makeup,

00:04:48.954 --> 00:04:50.289
and then you style them,

00:04:50.289 --> 00:04:52.358
and then you do, like,
fashion shows around the pool,

00:04:52.358 --> 00:04:54.594
and people vote to see
who did it better.

00:04:54.594 --> 00:04:56.029
[ Laughter ]

00:04:56.029 --> 00:05:00.099
-See, I can't do my daughters'
nails even not blindfolded.

00:05:00.099 --> 00:05:01.167
[ Laughter ]

00:05:01.167 --> 00:05:02.669
-No. It's an impossible task.
-Oh, yes.

00:05:02.669 --> 00:05:04.137
-Like, I think
that's kind of the point.

00:05:04.137 --> 00:05:06.673
I just draw on her face
with everything.

00:05:06.673 --> 00:05:07.840
I just --

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:09.975
-And she does that to you.
Yeah, it's fun.

00:05:09.975 --> 00:05:11.944
I love the message
behind the book,

00:05:11.944 --> 00:05:13.946
and congrats,
and I'm glad you wrote this.

00:05:13.946 --> 00:05:15.414
Congratulations, buddy.
-Thank you, man.

00:05:15.414 --> 00:05:16.616
-Channing Tatum.

00:05:16.616 --> 00:05:20.553
"The One and Only Sparkella"
is available now.

